On Nov 19, 4:14 am, Topi Linkala <n...@iki.fi> wrote:
> > Polymorph and oil are rare, but that's clearly by design.
>
> Did you know that weak monsters might get
> potion of polymorph in their initial inventory.

I'd forgotten that.  For some reason, I never
seem to get potions of polymorph that way.
This was interesting to me, so I decided to
explore it.

So I did some checking, and it seems like
the following monsters are weak enough to
qualify:

* various weak animals (drfx:;BSsYqaup)
  will not receive it as they are animals.
  I'm not sure whether this also applies
  to wererats and werejackals.
* zombies, lichens, molds, fungi, blobs,
  oozes, shreikers, jellies, paper and straw
  golems, fog clouds, ghouls, lights,
  and kobold and gnome mummies
  will not receive it as they are mindless.
* gas spores will not receive it because
  they explode.
* K are ineligible for it as a special case.
* manes, in my experience, never receive
  inventory of any kind, though I cannot
  find documentation for this.
* humans can receive it, but they only
  occur in exotic circumstances.

So that leaves most o, all k, naga hatchlings,
hobbits, most G, dwarves, homunculi, imps,
lemures, leprechauns, nymphs, bugbears,
and floating eyes, all of which theoretically
can receive a potion of polymorph.  That's
quite a list, and some of those monsters
are rather common.

However, their monster level must exceed
a roll of d100 to get a miscellaneous item
(this excludes goblins and kobolds at level
one), and if it does they get a (1/30)*(5/6)
chance of getting the potion of polymorph,
which comes to 1/36.

The ones with a difficulty of 5 (bugbears,
Mordor orcs and Uruk-hai, nymphs, and
lemures) have the best chance,
(4/100)*(1/36) = 1/900.

For comparison, the same monsters'
chance of getting a potion of gain level is
(4/100)*(35/36)*(39/40)*(1/3) = 273/21600
That's a little better than 1/79.

A pit fiend's chance of getting a potion
of gain level is
(15/100)*(39/40)*(1/3) = 39/800,
which is just a shave less than 1/20.

Hobbits, large kobolds, and humans, at
level 2, have the worst non-zero chance
of getting a potion of polymorph,
(1/100)*(1/36) = 1/3600.


